m was samen.\nDutch tezamen (“together”) has been formed in a similar fashion, with its contracted form being samen and its ancestral form tsamen. Also cognate with Scots samin (“together”), Danish sammen (“together”), Swedish samman (“together”).","etymology_links":[["zesamene","zesamene#Middle_High_German"],["zesamne","zesamne#Middle_High_German"],["zesamen","zesamen#Middle_High_German"],["zisamane","zisamane#Old_High_German"],["zu-","zu-#German"],["sammen","sammen#German"],["sammen","sammen#German"],["*saman","Reconstruction:Proto-West Germanic/saman"],["*samanai","Reconstruction:Proto-Germanic/samanai"],["*sem-","Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/sem-"],["tosamen","tosamen#Low_German"],["tosamen","tosamen#Middle_English"],["sam","sam#English"],["samen","samen#English"],["tezamen","tezamen#Dutch"],["samen","samen#Dutch"],["tsamen","tsamen#Middle_Dutch"],["samin","samin#Scots"],["sammen","sammen#Danish"],["samman","samman#Swedish"]],"etymology_templates":[{"name":"inh","args":{"1":"de","2":"gmh","3":"zesamene, zesamne, zesamen","4":"","5":"together"},"expansion":"Middle High German zesamene, zesamne, zesamen (“together”)"},{"name":"inh","args":{"1":"de","2":"goh","3":"zisamane","4":"","5":"together"},"expansion":"Old High German zisamane (“together”)"},{"name":"prefix","args":{"1":"de","2":"zu","3":"sammen","4":"","t1":"to","t2":"together"},"expansion":"zu- (“to”) + sammen (“together”)"},{"name":"der","args":{"1":"de","2":"gmw-pro","3":"*saman"},"expansion":"Proto-West Germanic *saman"},{"name":"der","args":{"1":"de","2":"gem-pro","3":"*samanai","4":"","5":"together"},"expansion":"Proto-Germanic *samanai (“together”)"},{"name":"der","args":{"1":"de","2":"ine-pro","3":"*sem-","4":"","5":"together, one"},"expansion":"Proto-Indo-European *sem- (“together, one”)"},{"name":"cog","args":{"1":"nds","2":"tosamen","t":"together"},"expansion":"Low German tosamen (“together”)"},{"name":"cog","args":{"1":"enm","2":"tosamen","t":"together"},"expansion":"Middle English tosamen